From f9114e0756853f6df9d84a7ea9bd2442f1ec0fff Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ms178 <ms178@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 11:04:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] x86-64 peephole: compare-branch fusion flags-reader guard
 + register relays

Two changes to fuse_compare_and_branch:

* Soundness (latent miscompile): the fusion replaces
  `setCC; testq %rax; jCC target` with a direct `jCC' target` that
  reads the PRODUCER cmp's flags. The fall-through path previously
  carried the DROPPED testq's flags; any reader (cmov, setCC, adc,
  sbb, a conditional jump, pushfq) on the fall-through before the next
  full flag writer now observes the wrong flag state. The pass refuses
  the fusion when such a reader is in the observation window (64
  lines). inc/dec deliberately do not end the window: they preserve
  CF, so a later adc would still see the fused cmp's carry.

* New capability: the boolean relay may now land in any register
  (`setCC %al; movzbq %al, %rX; testq %rX, %rX; jCC`) - RA-homed
  booleans previously blocked the fusion entirely. Non-rax carriers
  are gated on exact FileLiveness: both the carrier and %rax must be
  provably dead after the fused jump, since their definitions are
  being removed. The legacy rax path keeps its corpus-validated
  contract. A rax test after a non-rax relay is still a different
  value and refuses to fuse (zlib-ng zng_deflateSetParams shape,
  pinned by an existing test).
